{"command": "cd /testbed && cat > specs/001-transactions/spec.md << 'SPEC_EOF'\n# Feature Specification: TaggedCache — Tagged Bounded Caching\n\n**Feature Branch**: `001-tagged-cache`\n\n**Created**: 2026-09-18\n\n**Status**: Draft\n\n**Input**: User description: \"Build cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache(maxsize), using the existing cachetools.LRUCache for bounded storage and preserving all existing cachetools APIs.\"\n\n## User Scenarios & Testing\n\n### User Story 1 — Tagged Entry Insertion and Retrieval (Priority: P1)\n\nA developer wants to cache values with tags so they can later invalidate entries by tag. They insert entries with `put(key, value, tags=())` and retrieve them with `get(key)`, receiving a deep copy of the stored value.\n\n**Why this priority**: This is the core functionality — without put/get, the cache is unusable.\n\n**Independent Test**: Create a TaggedCache, put an entry with a tag, get it back, verify the returned value is a deep copy (modifying it does not affect the cache), and verify the entry is present.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** an empty TaggedCache with maxsize=2, **When** I call `cache.put('a', [1, 2], tags=['x'])`, **Then** the entry is stored with key 'a', value [1, 2], and tag 'x'.\n2. **Given** the above entry, **When** I call `result = cache.get('a')`, **Then** result is `[1, 2]` (a deep copy) and modifying `result` does not change the cached value.\n3. **Given** an empty TaggedCache, **When** I call `cache.get('missing')`, **Then** it raises `KeyError`.\n\n---\n\n### User Story 2 — Tag-Based Invalidation (Priority: P1)\n\nA developer wants to remove all cached entries that carry a specific tag, returning the count of removed entries.\n\n**Why this priority**: Tag-based invalidation is the key differentiator of TaggedCache vs plain LRUCache.\n\n**Independent Test**: Insert two entries with the same tag, invalidate by that tag, verify both are removed and the count is 2.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** entries with tags ['x'] and ['y'], **When** I call `count = cache.invalidate('x')`, **Then** count equals the number of entries that had tag 'x' and those entries are no longer in the cache.\n2. **Given** no entries with tag 'z', **When** I call `cache.invalidate('z')`, **Then** count is 0.\n3. **Given** an entry replaced via `put(key, new_value, ['new'])`, **When** I call `cache.invalidate('old')` (the old tag), **Then** count is 0 — the old tag membership is removed.\n\n---\n\n### User Story 3 — LRU Eviction with Tagged Entries (Priority: P2)\n\nA developer expects that when the cache exceeds maxsize, the least recently used entries are evicted. Eviction must not leave stale tag memberships. `get()` refreshes LRU recency.\n\n**Why this priority**: Bounded storage is a core cache contract; stale tag memberships cause incorrect invalidation.\n\n**Independent Test**: Fill cache to maxsize, insert one more to trigger eviction, verify the correct entry is evicted, and verify that invalidated-by-tag counts are correct after eviction.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** a TaggedCache(maxsize=2) with entries 'a' and 'b', **When** I call `cache.get('a')` (refreshes recency), **When** I call `cache.put('c', 3, ['x'])`, **Then** entry 'b' is evicted (least recently used) and 'a' and 'c' remain.\n2. **Given** the above, **When** I call `cache.invalidate('x')`, **Then** count is 1 (only 'c').\n\n---\n\n### User Story 4 — Input Validation and Error Handling (Priority: P2)\n\nA developer expects that invalid inputs to `put()` are rejected with `ValueError` before any state change, and that `maxsize` must be a positive integer (not a bool).\n\n**Why this priority**: Defensive input validation prevents silent corruption and unexpected behavior.\n\n**Independent Test**: Pass a bare string as tags, a list with non-string entries, and a bool as maxsize — all must raise ValueError without mutating state.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `cache.put('k', 'v', tags='x')` (bare string), **Then** ValueError is raised and the cache is unchanged.\n2. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `cache.put('k', 'v', tags=[1, 2])` (non-string entries), **Then** ValueError is raised and the cache is unchanged.\n3. **Given** a TaggedCache, **When** I call `TaggedCache(maxsize=True)`, **Then** ValueError is raised.\n4. **Given** a valid TaggedCache(maxsize=5), **When** I attempt to set maxsize to an invalid value, **Then** ValueError is raised and the old maxsize remains.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- **Duplicate tags**: `put('k', 'v', tags=['x', 'x'])` — tags are deduplicated to `['x']`.\n- **Empty tags**: `put('k', 'v', tags=())` — valid; entry has no tags.\n- **Generator as tags**: `put('k', 'v', tags=(t for t in ['a', 'b']))` — must be accepted (finite iterable) and deduplicated.\n- **Replacing key with different tags**: Old tag memberships are removed; new tags are assigned.\n- **LRU eviction of a key that was previously invalidated by tag**: No stale tag references remain.\n- **len(cache)**: Counts only live (non-evicted, non-invalidated) entries.\n- **Values cost one slot**: Regardless of object size, each value occupies one capacity slot.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001**: TaggedCache MUST instantiate with a `maxsize` parameter that is a positive integer (type `int`, not `bool`). Invalid values raise `ValueError` before any state mutation.\n- **FR-002**: `put(key, value, tags=())` MUST insert or replace a cached entry. On replacement, old tag memberships for the key are removed.\n- **FR-003**: `get(key)` MUST return a detached deep copy of the stored value. If the key is missing, it MUST raise `KeyError`. A successful `get()` refreshes LRU recency.\n- **FR-004**: `invalidate(tag)` MUST remove all currently cached entries that carry the specified tag and return the count of removed entries.\n- **FR-005**: Tags MUST be validated as a finite iterable of strings. A bare string passed as `tags` MUST raise `ValueError`. Non-string entries in the tags iterable MUST raise `ValueError`. Validation occurs before any state mutation.\n- **FR-006**: Tags MUST be deduplicated within a single `put()` call.\n- **FR-007**: Values MUST be deep-copied on input (`put`) and on output (`get`).\n- **FR-008**: TaggedCache MUST use `cachetools.LRUCache` as its bounded storage backend.\n- **FR-009**: LRU eviction MUST remove entries from tag membership indexes so that no stale references persist. After eviction, `invalidate(tag)` must not count evicted entries.\n- **FR-010**: `len(cache)` MUST return the count of currently live (non-evicted, non-invalidated) entries.\n- **FR-011**: Each value MUST cost exactly one capacity slot regardless of object size.\n- **FR-012**: Replacing `maxsize` with an invalid value MUST leave the existing maxsize, tag memberships, and LRU recency unchanged.\n\n### Key Entities\n\n- **TaggedCache**: A bounded cache extending cachetools.LRUCache, storing key-value pairs with associated string tags. Provides put, get, invalidate, and len operations.\n- **Tag**: A string label attached to a cached entry. Used for batch invalidation. Deduplicated per entry.\n- **LRUCache Backend**: The underlying cachetools.LRUCache instance providing bounded storage and LRU eviction semantics.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Measurable Outcomes\n\n- **SC-001**: All existing cachetools public APIs (LRUCache, FIFOCache, TTLCache, cached, cachedmethod, etc.) continue to function unchanged after TaggedCache is added.\n- **SC-002**: TaggedCache put/get/invalidate operations complete in O(1) average time for standard operations.\n- **SC-003**: 100% of acceptance tests in acceptance_public.py pass without modification.\n- **SC-004**: All upstream cachetools tests continue to pass after TaggedCache integration.\n- **SC-005**: Deep copy isolation verified: modifying the value returned by `get()` never affects the value stored in the cache.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- TaggedCache is a new module at `src/cachetools/tagged.py` and is added to the package without modifying existing modules.\n- The `copy.deepcopy` function from the Python standard library is used for deep-copying values.\n- \"Finite iterable\" for tags means the iterable can be fully consumed without raising an exception (e.g., lists, tuples, sets, generators that terminate).\n- LRU recency semantics are inherited directly from cachetools.LRUCache.\n- The `getsizeof` parameter from the Cache base class is not used; each value costs one slot.\n- Public API additions include exporting `TaggedCache` from `cachetools.tagged` module.\nSPEC_EOF", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": ""}